    <string name="hint_line_width">How thick each streak is. Size variation makes some thicker or thinner than this.</string>
    <string name="hint_opacity">How bright each streak is. Above 1, overlapping streaks blend into solid color.</string>
    <string name="hint_trail_decay">How long trails last. Lower fades them faster: 0.65 is very short, 0.999 leaves long smears.</string>
    <string name="hint_wind_speed">How fast particles travel. Faster also means longer streaks, unless trails follow wind speed.</string>
    <string name="hint_particle_count">How many particles exist at once. The biggest factor for lag and battery.</string>
    <string name="hint_particle_life">Average seconds a particle lives before it fades out and reappears somewhere else.</string>
    <string name="hint_variation">Gives each particle its own speed, brightness, and lifetime. 0 makes them identical.</string>
    <string name="hint_size_variation">How different particle widths are. At 1, the smallest are about a fifth of the line width and the biggest several times it.</string>
    <string name="hint_size_style">How sizes are picked. Even: spread evenly. Rare giants: mostly small, a few big. Two sizes: small and big, nothing between.</string>
    <string name="hint_clumping">Makes particles appear more in some areas than others: dense currents and empty patches that drift over time.</string>
    <string name="hint_real_wind">How much the real wind map steers particles. At 0 it\'s ignored and only turbulence moves them.</string>
    <string name="hint_turbulence">Adds swirls that slowly reshape over time. Higher makes them stronger.</string>
    <string name="hint_swirl_size">Size of the swirls, warp, and clumping areas. Above 1: bigger, lazier shapes. Below 1: small, busy eddies.</string>
    <string name="hint_evolution">How fast the swirls, warp, and clumping change. 0 freezes them in place.</string>
    <string name="hint_warp">Bends and drifts the real wind\'s currents so they don\'t stay in the same place.</string>
    <string name="hint_momentum">How long particles take to change direction. Higher gives smoother, wider curves.</string>
    <string name="hint_buoyancy">Each particle slowly rises or sinks by its own amount.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_cycle">Scrolls the colors along the gradient. Higher is faster, negative reverses, 0 keeps them still.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_threshold">Wind speed where streaks start taking the colors. Lower colors more streaks.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_range">How much faster the wind gets between the first and last gradient color.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_opacity">Minimum brightness of colored gusts, so they stand out.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_firefly_amount">Fraction of particles that are fireflies.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_firefly_size">Glow size, as a multiple of the line width.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_pulse_rate">How many times a second each firefly pulses. Each one varies a little.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_pulse_sharpness">High: short blinks. Low: slow, soft breathing.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_snow_size">Flake size, as a multiple of the line width.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_snow_variation">How different flake sizes are from each other.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_fall">How fast flakes fall, on top of the wind.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_snow_softness">0: crisp dots. 1: soft, fuzzy flakes.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_snow_amount">Fraction of particles that are flakes. At 1 there are no streaks, only snow.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_fade">How gradually flakes appear and disappear. 0 is quick, 1 is very slow.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_head_size">Size of the comet head, as a multiple of the line width.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_white_core">How white-hot the center of the head is.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_tail_length">Trail length while comets are on. This also stretches the other streaks.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_halo">Size and strength of the glow around the head, in the opposite gradient color.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_ink_width">How much wider ink strokes are than normal streaks.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_linger">How much longer ink trails stay. This also stretches the other streaks.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_ink_softness">How blurry the stroke edges are.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_density">How solid the ink looks.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_radius">How far the glow spreads around the streaks.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_brightness">How strong the glow is.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_quality">Fast does half the work per pixel. Use it if neon makes things lag.</string>
    <string name="hint_fx_neon_pulse">How much the glow slowly brightens and dims, every 8 seconds.</string>
